## 34e41cf35fde

**Reproduced curriculum shortcut plus generator-contract defects; audit target left unchanged.** The audited generator SHA-256 is `ba87c1ba595b7fdcb1ea6473c9f3db36a2837f6337480081ce605a5e8d94ea20`; the selected Racket rule hash is `88e163b0ffa8`.

The rival “recolor the red component with the greatest top row” fits **3/3 canonical pairs** and **1,000/1,000** probed ordinary draws (250 each in default/easy/medium/hard). The ordinary constructor vertically stratifies the selected object, so greatest top row and greatest bottom row never conflict in the sample.

A lawful 10×10 counterexample places a tall red vertical object at rows 4–8, column 1, and a single red cell at `(7,7)`. The intended lowest-bottom rule recolors the tall left object; the top-row rival recolors the right singleton. `self_check` returns `[]`, the input obeys the documented palette/object domain, and supported Racket execution differs from the rival at six cells.

Evidence:

- `checks/audit/34e41cf35fde/shortcut/counterexample.json` — exact input, outputs, canonical/generated denominators, hashes, validator status, and differing cells;
- `checks/audit/34e41cf35fde/shortcut/racket.json` — supported authority receipt;
- `checks/audit/34e41cf35fde/shortcut/rival.json` — rival output;
- `checks/audit/34e41cf35fde/battery/result.json` — baseline battery.

The independent battery completed with **3 failed**, **2 advisory**, and **7 green** stages. Blocking findings include missing `RULE_HASH`, dead/overlapping texture controls, weak self-check behavior, thousands of undeclared multi-axis rejections, and silent acceptance of an unknown override key. These contract defects are separate from the semantic shortcut. No source was edited.
